Feature Flags (Feature Toggles): Runtime switches to enable/disable features without deploying. Use cases: Gradual rollout, A/B testing, kill switch, trunk-based development.

**Implementation with LaunchDarkly**

```java
// Dependencies
<dependency>
  <groupId>com.launchdarkly</groupId>
  <artifactId>launchdarkly-java-server-sdk</artifactId>
  <version>6.2.0</version>
</dependency>

// Configuration
@Configuration
public class FeatureFlagConfig {
  @Bean
  public LDClient ldClient(@Value("${launchdarkly.sdk-key}") String sdkKey) {
    LDConfig config = new LDConfig.Builder()
      .events(
        Components.sendEvents()
          .flushInterval(Duration.ofSeconds(5))
      )
      .build();

    return new LDClient(sdkKey, config);
  }
}

// Feature Flag Service
@Service
public class FeatureFlagService {
  @Autowired
  private LDClient ldClient;

  public boolean isFeatureEnabled(String featureKey, User user) {
    // Create LaunchDarkly user context
    LDContext context = LDContext.builder(user.getId())
      .set("email", user.getEmail())
      .set("country", user.getCountry())
      .set("accountType", user.getAccountType())
      .build();

    return ldClient.boolVariation(featureKey, context, false);
  }

  public <T> T getFeatureValue(String featureKey, User user, T defaultValue, Class<T> type) {
    LDContext context = buildContext(user);

    if (type == String.class) {
      return type.cast(ldClient.stringVariation(featureKey, context, (String) defaultValue));
    } else if (type == Integer.class) {
      return type.cast(ldClient.intVariation(featureKey, context, (Integer) defaultValue));
    } else if (type == Double.class) {
      return type.cast(ldClient.doubleVariation(featureKey, context, (Double) defaultValue));
    }

    return defaultValue;
  }
}

// Usage in Service
@Service
public class OrderService {
  @Autowired
  private FeatureFlagService featureFlags;

  @Autowired
  private NewCheckoutService newCheckoutService;

  @Autowired
  private LegacyCheckoutService legacyCheckoutService;

  public CheckoutResult checkout(Order order, User user) {
    // Feature flag: enable new checkout for 10% of users
    boolean useNewCheckout = featureFlags.isFeatureEnabled(
      "new-checkout-flow",
      user
    );

    if (useNewCheckout) {
      log.info("Using new checkout flow for user: {}", user.getId());
      return newCheckoutService.process(order);
    } else {
      return legacyCheckoutService.process(order);
    }
  }

  // Multivariate flag (A/B/C testing)
  public PaymentResult processPayment(Payment payment, User user) {
    String paymentStrategy = featureFlags.getFeatureValue(
      "payment-optimization",
      user,
      "default",
      String.class
    );

    switch (paymentStrategy) {
      case "fast-path":
        // Variant A: Skip some validations
        return fastPaymentProcessor.process(payment);
      case "extra-validation":
        // Variant B: Extra fraud checks
        return securePaymentProcessor.process(payment);
      default:
        // Control group
        return standardPaymentProcessor.process(payment);
    }
  }

  // Operational flag (kill switch)
  public List<Product> getRecommendations(User user) {
    boolean recommendationsEnabled = featureFlags.isFeatureEnabled(
      "ml-recommendations",
      user
    );

    if (recommendationsEnabled) {
      try {
        return mlRecommendationService.getRecommendations(user);
      } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("ML service failed, falling back", e);
        // Turn off flag remotely if ML service has issues
        return fallbackRecommendations();
      }
    } else {
      return fallbackRecommendations();
    }
  }
}
```

**Simple In-House Implementation**

```java
// Feature flag entity
@Entity
public class FeatureFlag {
  @Id
  private String key;

  private boolean enabled;

  @ElementCollection
  @CollectionTable(name = "feature_flag_rules")
  private List<RolloutRule> rules = new ArrayList<>();

  // User targeting rules
  @ElementCollection
  private Set<String> allowedUserIds = new HashSet<>();

  @ElementCollection
  private Set<String> allowedCountries = new HashSet<>();

  private int rolloutPercentage = 0; // 0-100
}

@Embeddable
public class RolloutRule {
  private String attribute; // "country", "accountType", etc.
  private String operator;  // "equals", "contains", "in"
  private String value;
}

// Repository
@Repository
public interface FeatureFlagRepository extends JpaRepository<FeatureFlag, String> {
}

// Service with caching
@Service
public class SimpleFeatureFlagService {
  @Autowired
  private FeatureFlagRepository repository;

  @Cacheable(value = "featureFlags", key = "#featureKey")
  public FeatureFlag getFlag(String featureKey) {
    return repository.findById(featureKey)
      .orElse(new FeatureFlag(featureKey, false));
  }

  public boolean isEnabled(String featureKey, User user) {
    FeatureFlag flag = getFlag(featureKey);

    if (!flag.isEnabled()) {
      return false;
    }

    // Check explicit allow list
    if (flag.getAllowedUserIds().contains(user.getId())) {
      return true;
    }

    // Check country targeting
    if (!flag.getAllowedCountries().isEmpty() && 
        !flag.getAllowedCountries().contains(user.getCountry())) {
      return false;
    }

    // Check rules
    for (RolloutRule rule : flag.getRules()) {
      if (!evaluateRule(rule, user)) {
        return false;
      }
    }

    // Percentage rollout (consistent hashing)
    if (flag.getRolloutPercentage() < 100) {
      int hash = Math.abs((featureKey + user.getId()).hashCode()) % 100;
      return hash < flag.getRolloutPercentage();
    }

    return true;
  }

  private boolean evaluateRule(RolloutRule rule, User user) {
    String userValue = getUserAttribute(user, rule.getAttribute());

    switch (rule.getOperator()) {
      case "equals":
        return rule.getValue().equals(userValue);
      case "contains":
        return userValue != null && userValue.contains(rule.getValue());
      case "in":
        Set<String> values = Set.of(rule.getValue().split(","));
        return values.contains(userValue);
      default:
        return false;
    }
  }
}

// Admin API to control flags
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/admin/feature-flags")
public class FeatureFlagController {
  @Autowired
  private FeatureFlagRepository repository;

  @Autowired
  private CacheManager cacheManager;

  @PostMapping("/{key}/enable")
  public void enableFlag(@PathVariable String key) {
    FeatureFlag flag = repository.findById(key)
      .orElse(new FeatureFlag(key, false));

    flag.setEnabled(true);
    repository.save(flag);

    // Clear cache
    cacheManager.getCache("featureFlags").evict(key);
  }

  @PostMapping("/{key}/rollout")
  public void setRolloutPercentage(
    @PathVariable String key,
    @RequestParam int percentage
  ) {
    FeatureFlag flag = repository.findById(key)
      .orElseThrow();

    flag.setRolloutPercentage(Math.min(100, Math.max(0, percentage)));
    repository.save(flag);

    cacheManager.getCache("featureFlags").evict(key);
  }
}
```

**Gradual Rollout Strategy**

```markdown
## Week 1: Internal Testing (0%)
- Feature flag: OFF
- Deploy code to production
- Enable for internal employee accounts only
- Validate: no errors, metrics look good

## Week 2: Canary (1%)
- Rollout: 1% of users
- Monitor: error rate, latency, conversion
- Success criteria: Error rate < 0.1%, P99 latency < 500ms
- Rollback trigger: Error rate > 1%

## Week 3: Expand (5% → 10% → 25%)
- Increase every 2 days if metrics healthy
- Monitor business metrics (revenue, engagement)

## Week 4: Full Rollout (100%)
- Enable for all users
- Keep flag for 1 week (easy rollback)
- Remove flag after confidence builds
```

**Best Practices**

1. **Short-lived flags**: Remove after rollout complete
2. **Flag hygiene**: Delete old flags (technical debt)
3. **Monitoring**: Track flag usage, measure impact
4. **Default OFF**: Fail safe if flag service unavailable
5. **Consistent hashing**: Same user always gets same experience
6. **Kill switches**: Quick disable for issues
7. **Testing**: Test both flag ON and OFF states

Benefits: Decouple deploy from release, instant rollback, A/B testing, gradual rollout, trunk-based development.
